# Extensions excluded from filesystem traversal (HLR-005).
#
# One extension per line, with or without its leading dot; blank lines and
# lines beginning with '#' are ignored. Matching is case-insensitive, so a
# single entry covers ".PNG" as well as ".png".
#
# This list is data, not code: an extension is added or removed by editing
# this file, with no rebuild (HLR-005, HLR-060). It applies to the filesystem
# route only — the Git route excludes binary blobs by asking the repository
# what is binary, which needs no list at all (HLR-003).
#
# The list is deliberately about *form*, not about language support. A file
# whose extension maps to no language module is skipped later and reported as
# skipped (HLR-012), which is visible; excluding it here would make it
# vanish. Only files that are binary by construction belong below.

# Object code, libraries, and executables
.o
.obj
.a
.lib
.so
.dylib
.dll
.exe
.elf
.ko
.class
.wasm
.pyc
.pyo
.pdb

# Archives and compressed streams
.zip
.tar
.gz
.bz2
.xz
.zst
.7z
.rar
.jar
.war
.tgz

# Images
.png
.jpg
.jpeg
.gif
.bmp
.ico
.tif
.tiff
.webp

# Documents that are containers rather than text
.pdf
.doc
.docx
.xls
.xlsx
.ppt
.pptx
.odt
.ods

# Audio and video
.mp3
.mp4
.m4a
.wav
.flac
.ogg
.avi
.mkv
.mov

# Fonts
.ttf
.otf
.woff
.woff2
.eot

# Databases and disk images
.db
.sqlite
.sqlite3
.iso
.img
.dmg
